From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:32:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 12/40] Compare with saved: show the unsaved changes as a diff

A new read-only tab shows the diff between the file on disk (empty for an
untitled tab) and the unsaved text of the editor tab, rendered with the
git diff view: removed lines red, added green, with context. Unlike the
gutter marks it shows the deleted text.

Opened from File > Compare with saved and the editor's context menu,
disabled when the tab has no unsaved changes. The diff is a snapshot;
opening it again for the same tab refreshes and focuses its compare tab.
Session restore skips it like a git diff tab.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

